    {"method:_thread.RLock._recursion_count", "For internal use by reentrancy checks."},
    {"method:_thread.RLock._release_save", "For internal use by `threading.Condition`."},
    {"method:_thread.RLock.acquire", "Lock the lock.\n\n`blocking` indicates whether we should wait\nfor the lock to be available or not.  If `blocking` is False\nand another thread holds the lock, the method will return False\nimmediately.  If `blocking` is True and another thread holds\nthe lock, the method will wait for the lock to be released,\ntake it and then return True.\n(note: the blocking operation is interruptible.)\n\nIn all other cases, the method will return True immediately.\nPrecisely, if the current thread already holds the lock, its\ninternal counter is simply incremented. If nobody holds the lock,\nthe lock is taken and its internal counter initialized to 1."},
    {"method:_thread.RLock.locked", "Return a boolean indicating whether this object is locked right now."},
    {"method:_thread.RLock.release", "Release the lock.\n\nAllows another thread that is blocked waiting for the lock\nto acquire the lock.  The lock must be in the locked state,\nand must be locked by the same thread that unlocks it; otherwise a\n`RuntimeError` is raised.\n\nDo note that if the lock was acquire()d several times in a row by\nthe current thread, release() needs to be called as many times for\nthe lock to be available for other threads."},
    {"method:_thread._ExceptHookArgs.__reduce__", ""},
    {"method:_thread._ExceptHookArgs.__replace__", "Return a copy of the structure with new values for the specified fields."},
    {"method:_thread._ThreadHandle._set_done", ""},
    {"method:_thread._ThreadHandle.is_done", ""},
    {"method:_thread._ThreadHandle.join", ""},
    {"method:_thread.lock.__enter__", "Lock the lock."},
    {"method:_thread.lock.__exit__", "Release the lock."},
    {"method:_thread.lock._at_fork_reinit", ""},
    {"method:_thread.lock.acquire", "Lock the lock.\n\nWithout argument, this blocks if the lock is already locked\n(even by the same thread), waiting for another thread to release\nthe lock, and return True once the lock is acquired.\nWith an argument, this will only block if the argument is true,\nand the return value reflects whether the lock is acquired.\nThe blocking operation is interruptible."},
    {"method:_thread.lock.acquire_lock", "An obsolete synonym of acquire()."},
    {"method:_thread.lock.locked", "Return whether the lock is in the locked state."},
    {"method:_thread.lock.locked_lock", "An obsolete synonym of locked()."},
    {"method:_thread.lock.release", "Release the lock.\n\nAllows another thread that is blocked waiting for\nthe lock to acquire the lock.  The lock must be in the locked state,\nbut it needn't be locked by the same thread that unlocks it."},
    {"method:_thread.lock.release_lock", "An obsolete synonym of release()."},
